{
  "registryVersion": "2026.08.26",
  "reviewedAt": "2026-08-26",
  "inclusionPolicy": "Publicly reachable cell, antenna, transmitter, or licensed-radio-site data with coordinates or a documented coordinate-bearing export. Login, API-key, attribution, share-alike, non-commercial, and provider-specific terms are recorded but are not exclusion criteria.",
  "providers": [
    {
      "id": "opencellid",
      "name": "OpenCelliD",
      "authority": "Unwired Labs / OpenCelliD contributors",
      "homepage": "https://opencellid.org/",
      "scope": "Crowdsourced cellular cells with MCC/MNC/LAC/TAC/radio and estimated coordinates",
      "coverage": [
        "global"
      ],
      "adapter": "opencellid-csv",
      "verifiedAt": "2026-08-14",
      "access": {
        "mode": "registration-token",
        "loginRequired": true,
        "credentialEnv": "OPENCELLID_TOKEN",
        "credentialLane": "cell_opencellid",
        "registrationUrl": "https://opencellid.org/",
        "termsUrl": "https://wiki.opencellid.org/wiki/Server_usage_policy",
        "notes": "The token is a QUERY PARAMETER on both endpoints, never a header. `credentialLane` is where it actually lives on an SDN node: the machine-bound credential store, lane cell_opencellid. `credentialEnv` is retained because it is part of this package's published seam, but it is the LESSER path — a credential in the environment is a credential in every child process — and the node flow reads the lane, not the variable. Daily request limits apply, so verification probes are spent deliberately."
      },
      "license": {
        "name": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "url": "https://wiki.opencellid.org/wiki/Menu_map_view",
        "attribution": "OpenCelliD Project (https://opencellid.org/)"
      },
      "endpoints": [
        {
          "kind": "bulk",
          "url": "https://opencellid.org/ocid/downloads?token=<token>&type=full&file=cell_towers.csv.gz",
          "format": "csv-gz",
          "refresh": "daily",
          "verifiedAt": "2026-08-14",
          "notes": "CORRECTED 2026-08-14. This was https://opencellid.org/downloads.php with format csv-zip; both were wrong. That URL is a human HTML download PAGE (verified live: 200, text/html, 14,729 bytes) and the payload is GZIP, not ZIP. The real route was verified live unauthenticated the same day: token=INVALID -> 200, application/json, {\"status\":\"error\",\"message\":\"INVALID_TOKEN\"}, which proves the path, the parameter names and the token check. TRAP: a bad token answers 200 with JSON, not 4xx, so a consumer that hands the body straight to a gz decoder reports an expired credential as an empty register. ~40M cells; consumers are expected to collapse to sites rather than store per-cell."
        },
        {
          "kind": "api",
          "url": "https://opencellid.org/cell/getInArea",
          "format": "api-json",
          "refresh": "live",
          "verifiedAt": "2026-08-09",
          "notes": "GET ?key=<token>&BBOX=<latmin>,<lonmin>,<latmax>,<lonmax>&format=json|csv&limit=<n>. BBOX is lat,lon,lat,lon. Its CSV header is NOT the bulk export's: net->mnc, area->lac, cell->cellid, averageSignal->averageSignalStrength, and there is no updated column at all."
        }
      ],
      "fieldMap": {
        "mnc": "net",
        "lac": "area",
        "cellId": "cell",
        "rangeMeters": "range",
        "updatedAt": "updated",
        "createdAt": "created"
      }
    },
